# Canonical External Dependencies

RULE: When adding or updating an **external** (PyPI) dependency in any repo, use the version range from the canonical manifest. New packages must be added via the workspace pinning flow so the manifest stays the single source of truth.

WHY: Prevents version drift across 30+ repos; one global list (JSON + SVG) for visibility and tooling. Workspace-manifest.json pins internal/private repos; this manifest pins external packages.

SSOT: `unified-trading-pm/canonical-dependency-manifest.json` (generated from workspace-constraints.toml). Visual: `unified-trading-pm/CANONICAL_DEPENDENCY_MANIFEST.svg`.

CODEX: 06-coding-standards/dependency-management.md (§ Workspace-wide dependency pinning, § Canonical dependency manifest).

DO:
  Check canonical-dependency-manifest.json (or workspace-constraints.toml) before adding a dependency — use the listed version range.
  For a package not in the manifest: add it in one repo with a sensible range, then run resolve-canonical-versions.py → propagate --apply → generate_canonical_dependency_manifest.py so the manifest and SVG are updated.
  Run scripts from workspace root: resolve-canonical-versions.py, propagate-canonical-versions.py --apply, aggregate-workspace-deps.py --resolve, then scripts/manifest/generate_canonical_dependency_manifest.py.

NEVER:
  Add an external dependency with a version range that contradicts the canonical manifest without going through the resolve/propagate flow (and updating the manifest).
  Assume a package version — look it up in unified-trading-pm/canonical-dependency-manifest.json or workspace-constraints.toml.

See also: dependency-version-alignment.mdc (codex check); uv-lock-file.mdc (lock after changes).
